You know, so Biden's
taking Fauci's advice,

00:09:11.651 --> 00:09:13.553
but Fauci is the problem.

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:15.221
- So, I mean, I think I
know your answer to this,

00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:17.056 align:start size:84% position:16%
but should Fauci
should just step down?

00:09:17.056 --> 00:09:18.958
I mean, it doesn't seem
to me that this is a guy

00:09:18.958 --> 00:09:21.227 align:start size:84% position:16%
who should be running
the NIH anymore.

00:09:21.227 --> 00:09:23.129
I mean, enough's enough already.

00:09:23.129 --> 00:09:26.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
- I mean, if we don't have
room for him in prison,

00:09:26.032 --> 00:09:28.267
I mean, stepping down
would probably be okay.

00:09:28.267 --> 00:09:30.503 align:start size:84% position:16%
But no, he's a
menace in the sense

00:09:30.503 --> 00:09:35.508
that he really is careless and
callous towards our liberty.

00:09:36.876 --> 00:09:40.179 align:start size:97% position:3%
His first impulse is always
an authoritarian one.

00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:42.582
But he also ignores the science.

00:09:42.582 --> 00:09:46.118
So by conservative estimates,
over 100 million Americans

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:47.653
have gotten this.

00:09:47.653 --> 00:09:50.323
62 million, on the official
website, have gotten COVID.

00:09:50.323 --> 00:09:53.759
But the NIH has studies
that say five people,

00:09:53.759 --> 00:09:55.561 align:start size:97% position:3%
for every person
diagnosed, there's at least

00:09:55.561 --> 00:09:57.597
five people undiagnosed.

00:09:57.597 --> 00:09:58.898
Let's say it's only one or two.

00:09:58.898 --> 00:10:00.766 align:start size:84% position:16%
We still get to well
over 100 million,

00:10:00.766 --> 00:10:03.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
and maybe half of America
has been infected.

00:10:03.469 --> 00:10:05.271
If you don't count
them, then you think

00:10:05.271 --> 00:10:07.206 align:start size:81% position:19%
we're woefully
short on vaccines.

00:10:07.206 --> 00:10:09.041
Then you mandate it on children.

00:10:09.041 --> 00:10:10.309
But the other thing there,

00:10:10.309 --> 00:10:12.912
you would never know
this by watching CNN

00:10:12.912 --> 00:10:16.949 align:start size:97% position:3%
or any of these other networks
that are full of fake news,

00:10:16.949 --> 00:10:21.520
if you look at how many people
have been infected naturally

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:24.624 align:start position:0%
and you say, well, how many
people have gotten the vaccine?

00:10:24.624 --> 00:10:27.994 line:0%
95% of people over 65
have been vaccinated.

00:10:27.994 --> 00:10:30.763 line:0%
It's even higher
if you go above 75.

00:10:30.763 --> 00:10:34.634 line:0%
The voluntary vaccine has
been an enormous success.

00:10:34.634 --> 00:10:36.435
But if you watch CNN,
you think, oh gosh,

00:10:36.435 --> 00:10:37.903
nobody's been vaccinated.

00:10:37.903 --> 00:10:39.205
The truth is the opposite.

00:10:39.205 --> 00:10:41.073
Almost everybody that's
at risk for this disease

00:10:41.073 --> 00:10:42.475
has been vaccinated.

00:10:42.475 --> 00:10:44.076 align:start size:84% position:16%
The children are
getting it naturally,

00:10:44.076 --> 00:10:45.711 align:start size:84% position:16%
whether you vaccinate
them or not.

00:10:45.711 --> 00:10:48.381 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now adults are
getting it whether you
vaccinate them or not.

00:10:48.381 --> 00:10:51.083
Really we're headed towards
where there's going to be

00:10:51.083 --> 00:10:53.686 align:start size:84% position:16%
enough immunity
within the community,

00:10:53.686 --> 00:10:57.189 align:start position:0%
and I think the devolving nature
of this is towards a cold.

00:10:57.189 --> 00:10:59.792 align:start position:0%
We have four other
coronaviruses that cause a cold.

00:10:59.792 --> 00:11:02.194
This is going to become
the fifth coronavirus.

00:11:02.194 --> 00:11:03.729
The sooner the better.

00:11:03.729 --> 00:11:05.297 align:start size:88% position:13%
And then we also at
the same time will have

00:11:05.297 --> 00:11:07.166 align:start size:84% position:16%
some people dying,
the vulnerable people.

00:11:07.166 --> 00:11:10.670 align:start size:97% position:3%
Let's try to save them by
getting government obstacles

00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:13.406 align:start size:97% position:3%
out of the way so we can
have more monoclonals again,

00:11:13.406 --> 00:11:15.408
and more of the new pills.

00:11:15.408 --> 00:11:17.209 align:start size:88% position:13%
But also let's repurpose
some of the things

00:11:17.209 --> 00:11:19.879
that we have out there
that lessen inflammation.

00:11:21.347 --> 00:11:23.149
- I want to shift a little
bit to the big tech thing,

00:11:23.149 --> 00:11:24.417
and I know you're on
a time crunch here,

00:11:24.417 --> 00:11:26.118
but just one or two
more things on this.

00:11:26.118 --> 00:11:27.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
First off, obviously
you've been talking about

00:11:27.953 --> 00:11:31.223
libertarianism and individual
rights and the constitution,

00:11:31.223 --> 00:11:34.427
all of that old school stuff,
for years and years and years,

00:11:34.427 --> 00:11:35.795
and your dad before you.

00:11:35.795 --> 00:11:40.132
Are you sort of shocked
how this COVID thing

00:11:40.132 --> 00:11:43.135
has unmasked so many
of your colleagues,

00:11:43.135 --> 00:11:45.171 align:start size:97% position:3%
people that you maybe had
political disagreements with,

00:11:45.171 --> 00:11:48.340
but that just went
so all in on just

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.076 align:start size:88% position:13%
government,
government, government?

00:11:51.711 --> 00:11:54.013
- I guess I'm not very
excited about having

00:11:54.013 --> 00:11:57.616 align:start size:84% position:16%
some snot-nosed punk
over at Facebook

00:11:57.616 --> 00:12:00.886
or over at Twitter
or over at YouTube

00:12:00.886 --> 00:12:03.622
decide they're going
to judge the science.

00:12:05.024 --> 00:12:06.726 align:start size:97% position:3%
It took a little bit of effort
to get to medical school,

00:12:06.726 --> 00:12:08.194
it took a little bit of effort

00:12:08.194 --> 00:12:09.895 align:start position:0%
to get to one of the better
medical schools in the country.

00:12:09.895 --> 00:12:12.031
And I got some kids who's lucky

00:12:12.031 --> 00:12:13.466
if he has a journalism major,

00:12:13.466 --> 00:12:15.401
who's lucky if he ever
took a science class,

00:12:15.401 --> 00:12:17.603 align:start size:84% position:16%
doesn't know what
organic chemistry is,

00:12:17.603 --> 00:12:20.673 align:start size:97% position:3%
telling me that I'm
promulgating misinformation.

00:12:20.673 --> 00:12:22.608
So it's really insulting.

00:12:22.608 --> 00:12:26.212
But also on another level,
on a very personal level,

00:12:26.212 --> 00:12:28.314
these people despise us.

00:12:28.314 --> 00:12:29.915
We are the deplorables to them.

00:12:29.915 --> 00:12:32.284
We are the people who
live in flyover country

00:12:32.284 --> 00:12:35.454 align:start position:0%
and we are the people they
would look down their nose at us

00:12:35.454 --> 00:12:38.791
with contempt, so why do
we give them our content?

00:12:38.791 --> 00:12:41.026
This is what makes me
mad about conservatives

00:12:41.026 --> 00:12:42.495
and libertarians.

00:12:42.495 --> 00:12:43.662
They're all complaining,
saying, oh, I hate big tech

00:12:43.662 --> 00:12:44.864
and we should break them up.

00:12:44.864 --> 00:12:46.499 align:start size:84% position:16%
No, that's a big
government solution.

00:12:46.499 --> 00:12:48.033
Quit using them.

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:52.671
If we all quit using them,
we are 40% strong, at least.

00:12:53.873 --> 00:12:55.875
We're maybe closer to
50% of the country.

00:12:55.875 --> 00:12:57.143
If we quit using Twitter,

00:12:57.143 --> 00:12:59.145
we can topple them
instantaneously.

00:12:59.145 --> 00:13:03.549
Just my shift to Rumble, I
think is having an effect.

00:13:03.549 --> 00:13:06.352
But I'm one of maybe 10 or
20 prominent conservatives

00:13:06.352 --> 00:13:07.219
and libertarians up here.

00:13:07.219 --> 00:13:08.687
What if we all did it?

00:13:08.687 --> 00:13:11.323 align:start size:84% position:16%
I think we really
could have an effect.

00:13:11.323 --> 00:13:13.325
And the thing is is
I don't want people

00:13:13.325 --> 00:13:16.028
to make money off my content
who look at me with contempt

00:13:16.028 --> 00:13:18.197
and say, oh, we don't like
this, we don't like that.

00:13:18.197 --> 00:13:19.431
You can't publish this.

00:13:19.431 --> 00:13:20.933 align:start size:84% position:16%
Oh, you said this
on the Senate floor?

00:13:20.933 --> 00:13:24.570 align:start size:97% position:3%
Sorry, we're not going to
let you say that on YouTube.

00:13:24.570 --> 00:13:26.372 align:start size:84% position:16%
So yeah, I don't
want to be associated

00:13:26.372 --> 00:13:28.107
with close-minded people.

00:13:28.107 --> 00:13:30.976
- So to that point, you
officially have announced

00:13:30.976 --> 00:13:33.112
that you're moving all of
your content to Rumble.

00:13:33.112 --> 00:13:35.447
But it wasn't just that, you
did something kind of snarky.

00:13:35.447 --> 00:13:38.250
You basically said
I'll only use YouTube

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:41.153 align:start size:84% position:16%
to attack the
policies of YouTube,

00:13:41.153 --> 00:13:42.955
which I thought was a
pretty beautiful thing.

00:13:42.955 --> 00:13:45.090 align:start size:88% position:13%
I should just say for
full transparency's sake

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:47.126 align:start size:88% position:13%
that everyone knows
that Locals, my company,

00:13:47.126 --> 00:13:48.994
merged with Rumble, so
I have some interest

00:13:48.994 --> 00:13:50.563
in Rumble obviously.

00:13:50.563 --> 00:13:53.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is there anything the
government should be doing

00:13:53.532 --> 00:13:54.867
related to any of this?

00:13:54.867 --> 00:13:56.669 align:start position:0%
This is where the
libertarian/conservative divide

00:13:56.669 --> 00:13:57.903
always goes.

00:13:57.903 --> 00:13:59.438 align:start size:84% position:16%
We discussed it once
or twice before,

00:13:59.438 --> 00:14:01.774 align:start size:97% position:3%
but is there any room for
the government at any level,

00:14:01.774 --> 00:14:03.475
break them up, anything?

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:07.446
- I'll listen, but I'm
always sort of hesitant

00:14:07.446 --> 00:14:09.648 align:start size:88% position:13%
to believe the solution
is the government.

00:14:09.648 --> 00:14:12.718
I'm also a big believer in
unintended consequences.

00:14:12.718 --> 00:14:14.520 align:start size:88% position:13%
The more you look
carefully at a subject,

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:17.489
when the government
gets involved, the
unintended happens.

00:14:17.489 --> 00:14:19.191 align:start size:84% position:16%
One of the arguments
big tech says

00:14:19.191 --> 00:14:21.260
for not taking away liability

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:23.362 align:start size:88% position:13%
is that if you take away
liability protection

00:14:23.362 --> 00:14:25.431 align:start size:84% position:16%
that big tech enjoys,
what they'll do

00:14:25.431 --> 00:14:27.466
is become more censorious.

00:14:27.466 --> 00:14:29.101
They will censor more people

00:14:29.101 --> 00:14:30.603
because they don't
want to be sued.

00:14:30.603 --> 00:14:33.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there is some argument
for saying, you know,

00:14:33.439 --> 00:14:36.175
Dave Rubin called Rand
Paul this on Facebook.

00:14:36.175 --> 00:14:37.209
Let's sue Facebook.

00:14:37.209 --> 00:14:38.377
Well, that's ridiculous.

00:14:38.377 --> 00:14:40.012 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, if we're calling
each other names,

00:14:40.012 --> 00:14:41.747
either quit using them,
don't listen to them,

00:14:41.747 --> 00:14:44.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
turn them off, or call the
other guy a worse name.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:47.119 align:start size:84% position:16%
But if we get involved
with lawsuits,

00:14:47.119 --> 00:14:49.188
and people say, well, what
about the old fashioned,

00:14:49.188 --> 00:14:50.656
the established media?

00:14:50.656 --> 00:14:52.057
And here's my answer.

00:14:52.057 --> 00:14:53.826 align:start size:84% position:16%
Give them liability
protection too.

00:14:53.826 --> 00:14:55.694 align:start size:88% position:13%
Instead of taking away,
and this is sort of

00:14:55.694 --> 00:14:58.497
an outlier position, but
instead of taking away

00:14:58.497 --> 00:15:00.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
liability protection,
give it to the newspapers

00:15:00.666 --> 00:15:05.671
and the broadcast media as well,

00:15:06.538 --> 00:15:08.007
and I would go one step further.

00:15:08.007 --> 00:15:12.077
I would also let newspapers
and television organize,

00:15:13.512 --> 00:15:16.148
the bad for this is collude,
but I would let them organize

00:15:16.148 --> 00:15:18.584 align:start size:88% position:13%
to try to set the
prices for their content

00:15:18.584 --> 00:15:20.486
for YouTube and Facebook.

00:15:20.486 --> 00:15:23.122 align:start position:0%
The big complaint from old
media is they take our content.

00:15:23.122 --> 00:15:26.058 align:start size:97% position:3%
We hire reporters and writers
and we put all this money

00:15:26.058 --> 00:15:28.294 align:start size:84% position:16%
and effort into
writing up the news,

00:15:28.294 --> 00:15:31.430
and then it's stolen from us
and used by the big tech people

00:15:31.430 --> 00:15:33.032
who don't pay us
for our content.

00:15:33.032 --> 00:15:34.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, let all the
newspapers in the country

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:38.737
get together and negotiate
as one entity with Facebook.

00:15:38.737 --> 00:15:40.773
So there are ways
around some of this

00:15:40.773 --> 00:15:43.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
that are creative thinking
to try to equalize

00:15:43.342 --> 00:15:46.045 align:start size:84% position:16%
the playing field, but
I've never been for

00:15:46.045 --> 00:15:49.682 align:start size:97% position:3%
oh, so and so has less
regulations than this company.

00:15:49.682 --> 00:15:51.016
Do you want to equalize them?

00:15:51.016 --> 00:15:52.251
Let's lower the regulations.

00:15:52.251 --> 00:15:53.352 align:start size:84% position:16%
Let's don't increase
the regulations,

00:15:53.352 --> 00:15:54.787
do you know what I mean?

00:15:54.787 --> 00:15:58.090 align:start size:97% position:3%
Let's try to lower the burden
to equalize opportunity

00:15:58.090 --> 00:15:59.525
and access to markets.

00:15:59.525 --> 00:16:01.293
- So last thought, just
tying the COVID thing

00:16:01.293 --> 00:16:02.795
and the big tech thing together,

00:16:02.795 --> 00:16:04.730
I mean, do you really sense
that the future of America

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:06.899
is just gonna be sort
of parallel societies?

00:16:06.899 --> 00:16:10.469
Red states will operate one
way and, say, people like us

00:16:10.469 --> 00:16:12.404 align:start size:84% position:16%
will operate on
alternate platforms

00:16:12.404 --> 00:16:15.207 line:0%
that will not be the
mainstream platforms,

00:16:15.207 --> 00:16:19.244 line:0%
that everything is sort of
splitting, and I would argue

00:16:19.244 --> 00:16:23.248 line:0%
maybe that was the genius of
federalism in the first place,

00:16:23.248 --> 00:16:24.683
and it's all okay.

00:16:24.683 --> 00:16:27.619 align:start position:0%
- Yeah, well, particularly
when you federalize government,

00:16:27.619 --> 00:16:28.821
you have the different levels,

00:16:28.821 --> 00:16:30.356 align:start size:84% position:16%
you can kind of
move where you like.

00:16:30.356 --> 00:16:33.826
And you know, if you're into
the San Francisco lifestyle,

00:16:33.826 --> 00:16:36.495
you can live out there and
it's whatever goes goes.

00:16:36.495 --> 00:16:38.597
If you want to live
in the Bible belt

00:16:38.597 --> 00:16:40.632
and it's less accepting,
and in a small community

00:16:40.632 --> 00:16:42.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Oklahoma for that
lifestyle, you live there.

00:16:42.768 --> 00:16:45.270
And I think some of that is
good because then we can have

00:16:45.270 --> 00:16:48.273
sort of freedom of choice, of
lifestyle and everything else.

00:16:48.273 --> 00:16:50.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
We already have it a
little bit with marijuana

00:16:50.542 --> 00:16:51.810
and things like that.

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:54.246
In the more accepting
states, it's allowed,

00:16:54.246 --> 00:16:55.614 align:start size:84% position:16%
the other states
it's not yet allowed.

00:16:55.614 --> 00:16:57.649
And so people can
kind of gravitate,

00:16:57.649 --> 00:16:59.785 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the smaller the
denomination of government,

00:16:59.785 --> 00:17:01.720
the more freedom you can
have because, you know,

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:04.156
if it's a whole state, it's
expensive to leave the state,

00:17:04.156 --> 00:17:05.691
but if it's just your town.

00:17:05.691 --> 00:17:08.060 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, remember
when we had dry towns.

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:10.262
It was actually dangerous,
not that I ever did this,

00:17:10.262 --> 00:17:13.032
but you had to drive to the
other town and then back.

00:17:13.032 --> 00:17:15.000
Of course, some people
would open their bottle

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:17.536 align:start size:97% position:3%
on the way back, of course,
and that was a problem.

00:17:17.536 --> 00:17:19.004
- Not that you ever did this.

00:17:19.004 --> 00:17:21.340
- You had communities, and I
know you never did that either,

00:17:21.340 --> 00:17:25.077
but you had communities that
sort of made these decisions,

00:17:25.077 --> 00:17:26.378
and people could choose to live

00:17:26.378 --> 00:17:27.780
in the community they wanted to.

00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:30.182 align:start size:88% position:13%
And probably the smaller
the denomination,

00:17:30.182 --> 00:17:33.552
or the smaller the size of
the government, the better.

00:17:33.552 --> 00:17:35.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Senator, I know you
have to continue your day

00:17:35.687 --> 00:17:38.624 align:start position:0%
of smacking around Fauci, either
in the media or in person.

00:17:38.624 --> 00:17:41.994 align:start size:97% position:3%
I appreciate your time,
and I hope to see you soon.

00:17:41.994 --> 00:17:43.495
- Thank you.

